00:00:05.236 --> 00:00:07.020
SUDHEERA VANGURI: Hi, everyone.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:10.530
Welcome to the Document AI
session I am Sudheera Vanguri

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.240
and I lead the Document AI
product suite at Google Cloud.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.890
A quick run through
of the agenda

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.310
today, I'll be starting with
the challenges and market

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.240
opportunities we're seeing in
document processing and dive

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.250
into a product overview
of Document AI.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.730
I'll also be sharing
some customer use cases

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:31.250
and some exciting new
announcements in Document AI

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.950
solutions.

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:34.575
Following that, my
colleague, Lewis Liu

00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:36.340
will unbundle some
of the technologies

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.300
we use under the hood.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.350
Let's dive right in.

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:46.240
Nearly all the business
processes today begin, include,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.730
or end with a document.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:52.300
Most companies are sitting
on a document goldmine.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:57.910
Think PDFs, emails, customer
feedback, patents, contracts,

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.290
technical documents,
sensitive documents, HR files,

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.890
and the list goes on.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:08.350
And these documents are only
going to grow with time.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.200
If you're already trying to
make sense of your documents,

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.440
it's likely you're only
scratching the surface.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.950
A lot of these documents
are unstructured,

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:21.920
which can be very time
consuming to process.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.280
What do we mean by
structured and unstructured?

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:29.220
20% of enterprise
data is structured.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.400
Now by structured
data, this can be

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.700
human-generated or
machine-generated data

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:39.790
that is highly organized and
formatted to be searchable.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:43.570
A lot of data analytics
tools out there

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:48.340
can be used to process
structured data.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:53.530
However, 80% of enterprise data
today is still unstructured.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:56.710
This unstructured data is
in the form of free form

00:01:56.710 --> 00:02:00.820
text such as written
documents, emails, comments.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.220
And the data analytics
tools out there

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.400
to process this unstructured
data are still very nascent.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:14.920
Document processing has become
increasingly complex with time.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.760
Processes that involve large
volumes of unstructured content

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:20.500
are increasing day by day.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.080
For instance, top
tier logistics firms

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.160
process over 50,000
bills of ladings per day.

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:30.610
The diversity of incoming
data spans a variety

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.920
of doc types and formats.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.530
For instance, the average
mortgage application

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:43.540
today exceeds over 350 pages and
over 60 major document types.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.910
Why is the diversity increasing?

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:48.520
This diversity can
be increasing because

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:52.390
of government regulations,
and as the types of business

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.880
relationships and
entity linkages

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.130
across various [? all ?]
documents increase with time.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.980
A lot of external
knowledge can also

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:06.040
be associated with a document
in its evaluation process.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:07.680
For instance,
looking at a document

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.340
you may need to know if
this driver's license is

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:16.060
the official Nebraska driver's
license format or not.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:20.080
Cross linking entities within
various incoming data streams

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.150
generates major new value.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:26.050
And analyzing the semantic
depth of documents

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:29.680
can unlock various
insights within businesses.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:37.400
However, processing these
documents is quite challenging.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.290
Because of the various document
formats, the manual processes,

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:44.720
the costs of error,
a lot of bad data,

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.610
and long processing
times and delays,

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.870
businesses are faced with
high costs, lost revenue,

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.840
and missed opportunities.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.440
That's where
Document AI comes in.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:02.780
In a nutshell, Document AI
extracts structured data

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:06.420
from unstructured content.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:09.600
Document AI enables
businesses to unlock insights

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:12.540
from your documents
with machine learning.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.470
This can enable businesses
to make better decisions

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:19.470
such as analyzing customer
feedback, processing

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:23.470
invoices, or reduced
mortgage processing times.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:28.200
Document AI can extract as
well as classify information

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:29.970
from unstructured documents.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:37.070
Document AI within
Google Cloud builds

00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:40.850
on top of our computer vision,
natural language, and knowledge

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:42.470
graph technologies.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:46.460
We have a variety of products
within Google Cloud AI

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:51.230
to meet customers
where they are.

00:04:51.230 --> 00:04:53.780
Within Document
AI building blocks

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.840
we have a suite of products
under general Document

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:02.250
AI, custom Document AI, and
specialized Document AI.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:05.370
By general Document
AI, I'm referring

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:10.760
to Google's general OCR models
applied to your content.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:14.360
Custom Document AI enables
you to train custom models

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:19.400
on your content, to identify
domain specific content tuned

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.760
to your own specific
training data.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.580
With specialized
Document AI you can

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:29.030
use Google [? sturdy ?]
models to get out

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:31.640
of the box extraction and
classification for some

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.430
of the most common document
types in the world.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:38.310
Let me unbundle that for
you a little bit more.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:42.960
With general Document
AI we have our print OCR

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:48.990
and handwriting OCR APIs
that are already in GA.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:53.360
They support over 200
languages with our print OCR

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:57.060
and over 50 languages
with our handwriting OCR.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.810
These are already available
under the Vision API today.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:03.600
Recently, we have also
introduced the form parser

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.150
API in beta.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:09.420
And this enables you to
identify special content

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:13.590
such as key value pairs,
tabular content within highly

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:14.760
structured forms.

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:22.120
With custom Document
AI, last year

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:27.700
we went out GA with AutoML Doc
Classification and AutoML Doc

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.950
Extraction APIs.

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:34.420
These tools enable you to
provide your own training data

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:39.010
and tune domain specific
content, extraction,

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:44.460
and classification applied to
your own business documents.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:49.340
We're also introducing custom
form parser APIs in alpha

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:53.870
that can enable you to
extract content provided

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:55.750
a single blank form template.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.540
With our specialized
Document AI suite,

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:06.230
our goal is to catalog
and build dedicated models

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:09.860
for some of the world's
most common document types.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.760
These document models
are highly accurate,

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:16.940
enabling you to classify and
identify specific document

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:19.130
types such as
invoices and receipts

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.810
and various other
document types that I

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.030
will be talking about shortly.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:28.070
You can also provide data
validation and knowledge graph

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.717
validation against
dates, addresses,

00:07:30.717 --> 00:07:32.300
and various [INAUDIBLE]
types that you

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.820
find within these documents.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.590
And with this
turnkey capability,

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:40.430
you can apply these models to
do classification and extraction

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:44.230
against your own documents,
high volume documents

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.620
