With BigQuery, you could
perform more and advanced data

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:43.790
analytics, or just
like us, simply

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:46.670
look at the data in
the tabular format.

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:54.730
If we compare the
result side by side,

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:57.760
we actually extracted
values from the form

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:01.260
with high accuracy
and confidence.

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:04.710
Let's take a look
at a few of them.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:11.460
SSN, Social Security Number, all
nine digits match the document,

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:16.640
even though hyphens are
in the original field.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:19.129
Employer identification
number is also correct.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:25.470
And a more challenging
case, the employer name

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:31.530
and address on row number
six, the entire cell

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.945
also extracted 100% correct.

00:17:37.150 --> 00:17:40.120
Getting data extracted
from these two documents

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.010
is no easy task.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:44.730
Let me show you one of the
state-of-the-arts model we have

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.690
built at Google.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:51.440
Unlike classic NLP tasks,
document like invoices,

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.965
do not contain natural
language as you

00:17:53.965 --> 00:17:58.060
might find in regular
sentences and paragraphs.

00:17:58.060 --> 00:18:02.900
Data here is often
presented in tables.

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:07.600
In addition, many documents have
multiple pages, varying numbers

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:12.640
of sections, and have a variety
of layouts and formatting clues

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:15.550
to organize those informations.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:18.130
An understanding of
two dimensional layout

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:21.010
of the text on the
page is the key

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:24.350
to understanding such documents.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:28.130
Early this year, we publish a
new state-of-the-art research

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:33.170
paper on extracting data
from templatic documents.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:36.890
This technique is combined
with many things we learned

00:18:36.890 --> 00:18:40.820
and used from building optimal
natural language entity

00:18:40.820 --> 00:18:45.440
extraction models to better
understand receipts, bills,

00:18:45.440 --> 00:18:48.420
insurance quotes, and et cetera.

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:51.850
If you're interested in
learning more on this topic,

00:18:51.850 --> 00:18:56.490
I encourage you to take
a look at this paper.

